{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02G3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R \\to A$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-locally-P}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{definition-property-local}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-unramified}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:67cf4507ce762bf1f6488b552abeead965b267ab9753ff2db0fe1c35dd195d9e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c8680d9d91c184bd2958e88af9d6c6cc59cec91300156756e153bbf496eea876", "source_text": "This follows from Lemma <REF_0001> if we show that\nthe property ``<MATH_0001> is unramified'' is local.\nWe check conditions (a), (b) and (c) of Definition\n<REF_0002>.\nThese properties are proved in\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c608e42d6f30a5c92270528ae6932a0dcc0f9cf631160163fa388036ad12d7da", "unit_id": "tag:02G6:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02G3", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-composition-unramified}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:35ee04c18c28e593525552c3312d45ed0af3c5ae942a266a888115fbd5678655", "source_text": "The composition of two morphisms which are unramified is unramified.\nThe same holds for G-unramified morphisms.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:be126fab8da8f10c0590db3e51a446e19d9e4610a2e97f559c48e279a11c0ab3", "unit_id": "tag:02G9:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02G3", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-unramified-characterize}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-composition-type-P}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-unramified}", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c8fa25d15fb9b6c68dc160493ced30ffeef422864ce198f8953f50c43c084203", "source_text": "The proof of Lemma <REF_0001>\nshows that being unramified (resp.<SPACE_0001>G-unramified)\nis a local property of ring maps.\nHence the first statement of the lemma follows from\nLemma <REF_0002> combined\nwith the fact that being unramified (resp.<SPACE_0002>G-unramified)\nis a property of ring maps that is stable under composition, see\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f066f78cd69f66d25834893a661a88145682418ad4759125ac2245f7d2678344", "unit_id": "tag:02G9:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02G3", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-base-change-unramified}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e063d60d92b18ebe2f190a35aa71b8625398356a5486a4d6a8db6024213e22cf", "source_text": "The base change of a morphism which is unramified is unramified.\nThe same holds for G-unramified morphisms.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:580ab5e7e134753ca76be1328522d62b43c3f513b416f5f044875fab140bb018", "unit_id": "tag:02GA:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02G3", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-unramified-characterize}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-type-P}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-unramified}", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:940deed18a784014fff518ab02cdab8e8590418aad621194beb6e7e2ce35f261", "source_text": "The proof of Lemma <REF_0001>\nshows that being unramified (resp.<SPACE_0001>G-unramified)\nis a local property of ring maps. Hence the lemma follows from\nLemma <REF_0002> combined\nwith the fact that being unramified (resp.<SPACE_0002>G-unramified)\nis a property of ring maps that is stable under base change, see\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3e38506096d94e21d29eb19f6e0ced101883a80a7bc3df1321a390705e5ecd7c", "unit_id": "tag:02GA:proof"}
